course: dictionary
lesson: 5243
title: Words about luck
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A jinx is a person or thing that people believe brings bad luck. Jinx can also be a verb, to jinx something. Context helps you see which meaning is used. «Don't say we'll win, you'll jinx it!» The speaker is worried that saying the good news out loud will spoil the chance.
explain: The clues are «Don't say we'll win» and «you'll jinx it». They tell you the talk is about winning and that speaking about it might ruin it. So to jinx something means to bring bad luck to it. Check by swapping in "bring bad luck to": the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Jinx is also a shout in a children's game. When two friends say the same word at the same time, someone calls «Jinx!» That has nothing to do with bad luck. It is a game rule, so the words around it tell you which meaning to use.
fact: A jinx is a person or thing that people believe brings bad luck.
fact: To jinx something is to bring bad luck to it, often by talking about it too early.
fact: «Touch wood» and «jinx» are sayings people use as if words could bring luck or bad luck.
fact: There is no proof that jinxes are real; a jinx is a belief and a joke.
fact: In a game, «Jinx!» is called when two people say the same word at the same time.
exercise: «Don't say we'll win, you'll jinx it!» What does jinx mean here? | To make a loud noise | To win a race | *To bring bad luck to something | To forget a word
exercise: Two friends say "pizza" at the same time and one shouts «Jinx!» What does it mean in this game? | The game is over | *The two said the same word at the same time | Someone has bad luck forever | Pizza is banned
exercise: Is there proof that jinxes really change what happens? | Yes, but only in sport | Only on Fridays | *No, there is no proof; a jinx is a belief and a joke | Yes, scientists have proved it
test: In which sentence is jinx a verb, a doing word? | *Please don't jinx the trip by talking about the rain. | The jinx was blamed for the lost match. | Everyone knows the jinx is a silly belief. | She is a jinx on the team.
test: What do «touch wood» and «jinx» show about people? | They can change the weather with their voices | *They believe words can bring luck or bad luck | They only use these words in science class | They always know what will happen next
exam: Which is true about a jinx? | It is a word used only in sport | It is proved by scientists | It always brings good luck | *It is a belief that some people or things bring bad luck
